Derived data — Open Database License (ODbL) v1.0
================================================

The district bundles in this directory (PK*.json, index.json) are a DERIVED DATABASE.
They are produced by scripts/build_bundles.py from the sources below, and are published
under the Open Database License v1.0: https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

ODbL is share-alike. If you alter or build upon these bundles and distribute the result,
you must distribute it under ODbL too.

This is separate from the project's source code, which is MIT licensed (see ../../LICENSE).

Upstream sources contained in or derived into these files
---------------------------------------------------------

  School locations
    UNICEF Giga — https://maps.giga.global/
    Open Database License (ODbL). Credit: Giga and its contributors.
    Portions of that dataset are themselves derived from OpenStreetMap,
    © OpenStreetMap contributors, https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

    Overture Maps Foundation, places theme — https://overturemaps.org/
    CDLA-Permissive 2.0.

  Population
    Kontur Population Dataset (Pakistan), 400 m H3 hexagons
    https://data.humdata.org/dataset/kontur-population-pakistan
    Creative Commons Attribution (CC-BY).

  Relative wealth
    Meta Relative Wealth Index
    https://data.humdata.org/dataset/relative-wealth-index
    Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial (CC-BY-NC).
    NOTE: the NonCommercial condition applies to this component.

  Administrative boundaries
    OCHA Common Operational Datasets, Pakistan (ADM2)
    https://data.humdata.org/dataset/cod-ab-pak
    Creative Commons Attribution for Intergovernmental Organisations (CC-BY-IGO).

  Official school counts (used only as a denominator for the completeness ratio)
    Pakistan Institute of Education, Pakistan Education Statistics.

Because the ODbL component is share-alike, the combined derived database is distributed
under ODbL. The CC-BY-NC component means these bundles are not offered for commercial use.
